   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to certain reports\nprovided by the Long Island Power Authority",
    "basePrintNo": "S7778",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7778-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1020-kk, Pub Auth L (as proposed in S.1311-A & A.4635)",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7778\n\nSPONSOR: GAUGHRAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to certain\nreports provided by the Long Island Power Authority\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2021,\nc.765, to clarify provisions related to the Long Island Power Authori-\nty's service provider.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by clarifying that the\nLong Island Power Authority's service provider shall report on its\nlobbying and advertising activities on behalf of the Authority, in\nconnection with its management contract, or the operation of the Author-\nity's electric grid. The legislation also adds a provision to ensure\nthat the Long Island Power Authority or its service provider do not need\nto disclose any information that may otherwise be protected by law or\nregulation.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 765 of the Laws of 2021. S.1311A and A.4635\nboth passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in June 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2021 amending Public Authorities Law in relation\nto requiring the Long Island Power Authority to prepare a semi-annual\nexpenditure and lobbying report, as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S.1311-A and A.4635, takes effect.\n",
